// nn/ — layers, parameter containers and the composite models built on them.
//
// Sits above activ: conv2d, pooling and the norms compose the elementwise ops.
// It imports core directly as well, for sqrtf and the libm bindings the
// normalisation paths use.
//
// `tensor.mbt` is here rather than in core because its broadcast and softmax
// semantics are defined against the layer conventions -- 5D [T,B,C,H,W] for
// the convolutions, 2D for the classifier heads -- not against any arithmetic
// that would make it independent of them.
//
// `bottles.mbt` carries the Box-Muller transform, which is why it needs
// core's sqrtf/logf/sinf/cosf. Those four bindings all used to live in
// unrelated files; sqrtf in optimizer_adam.mbt, cosf in scheduler.mbt, sinf in
// bottles.mbt itself. Moving them into core/ is what let this package exist.
//
// neuron/ is imported only for `box_muller`, which is declared in
// neuron_iz.mbt yet called from 95 places across the tree -- ARIMA, BiLSTM, C51,
// DCGAN, DDPM among them. A Gaussian sampler is not part of an Izhikevich
// neuron, and keeping it there forces every package that draws noise to depend
// on the neuron package. Moving it down to core/ is the follow-up.
import {
  "riantr/snn_mbt/core",
  "riantr/snn_mbt/activ",
  "riantr/snn_mbt/neuron",
}
